# SPEC GOLDEN — hand-derived from css-flexbox-1 §5.2 and §9.6 before the code
# existed, never regenerated.
#
# `wrap-reverse` does one thing: it swaps cross-start and cross-end. For a row
# that means **cross-start is the bottom**, and everything else follows from
# that one sentence rather than from a second set of rules — lines stack from
# the bottom up, and every value that packs at cross-start packs downwards.
# Items are 160px = 20 cells; each is one line of text.
#
# Row 1 — six items, four to a line as in `spec/flex-wrap`. The *lines* are
#   what reversed, not the items: a b c d is still the first line and still
#   reads left to right, but it is now the lower of the two rows (y = 1) and
#   e f sits above it (y = 0). Reversing the items as well would need
#   `row-reverse`, which is a different property answering a different
#   question.
#
# Row 2 — `align-items: flex-start` **puts the items at the bottom of their
#   line**, which is the whole of what the flip means for alignment and reads
#   as a bug to anyone who has not met it. Both items fit on one line, the
#   container states 4 rows, and `align-content: stretch` (the initial value)
#   grows that one line to fill all 4 — so the line is the container's content
#   box and its cross-start edge is the container's bottom row, y = 5.
#
# Row 3 — `align-items: flex-end` is the same sentence from the other end: it
#   packs at cross-end, which is now the top, y = 6.
#
# Row 4 — `stretch`, the initial value, is the one alignment the flip cannot
#   move: an item that fills its line fills it from either end. The items are
#   4 rows tall and start at the line's top row, y = 10.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=14
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=14
    <div.rev> flex row wrap-reverse  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=2
      <div>  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=0 y=1 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=20 y=1 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=20 y=1 w=20 h=1
          line  x=20 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=20 y=1 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=40 y=1 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=40 y=1 w=20 h=1
          line  x=40 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "c"  x=40 y=1 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=60 y=1 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=60 y=1 w=20 h=1
          line  x=60 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "d"  x=60 y=1 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=1
            #text "e"  x=0 y=0 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=20 y=0 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=20 y=0 w=20 h=1
          line  x=20 y=0 w=20 h=1
            #text "f"  x=20 y=0 w=1 h=1
    <div.rev.tall.top> flex row wrap-reverse  x=0 y=2 w=80 h=4
      <div>  x=0 y=5 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=5 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=5 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=0 y=5 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=20 y=5 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=20 y=5 w=20 h=1
          line  x=20 y=5 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=20 y=5 w=1 h=1
    <div.rev.tall.bottom> flex row wrap-reverse  x=0 y=6 w=80 h=4
      <div>  x=0 y=6 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=6 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=6 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=0 y=6 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=20 y=6 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=20 y=6 w=20 h=1
          line  x=20 y=6 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=20 y=6 w=1 h=1
    <div.rev.tall> flex row wrap-reverse  x=0 y=10 w=80 h=4
      <div>  x=0 y=10 w=20 h=4
        anonymous  x=0 y=10 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=10 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=0 y=10 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=20 y=10 w=20 h=4
        anonymous  x=20 y=10 w=20 h=1
          line  x=20 y=10 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=20 y=10 w=1 h=1
